Description: Let Compiz screenshots start while fire painting holds its screen grab
 Ctrl+Shift+Button1 refused to start whenever any other plug-in held a screen
 grab, so drawing fire (Shift+Super+left drag, firepaint) silenced the Compiz
 screenshot path for the whole stroke.  firepaint only adds points and paints
 particles, and the core nests a second screen grab onto the one it already
 holds, so the capture works and includes the fire.
Author: Spaced Linux Developers <dev@spacedlinux.com>
Forwarded: no
--- a/plugins/screenshot.c
+++ b/plugins/screenshot.c
@@ -91,7 +91,13 @@
     {
 	SHOT_SCREEN (s);
 
-	if (otherScreenGrabExist (s, "screenshot", NULL))
+	/* Fire painting holds a screen grab for the whole stroke.  A capture
+	 * is still correct while that grab is held: pushScreenGrab nests onto
+	 * an existing grab and removeScreenGrab restores it, so only refuse
+	 * grabs belonging to another selection or movement plugin.  Without
+	 * this, Ctrl+Shift+Button1 does nothing at all while fire is drawn.
+	 */
+	if (otherScreenGrabExist (s, "screenshot", "firepaint", NULL))
 	    return FALSE;
 
 	if (!ss->grabIndex)
